# FIRST_VALUE() Cheat Sheet

```text
FIRST_VALUE(column)
        ↓
Take the value from the first row
        ↓
according to ORDER BY
```

### Lowest-paid employee

```sql
FIRST_VALUE(Name) OVER(
    PARTITION BY Department
    ORDER BY Salary ASC
)
```

### Highest-paid employee

```sql
FIRST_VALUE(Name) OVER(
    PARTITION BY Department
    ORDER BY Salary DESC
)
```

### Core concept

```text
PARTITION BY
    ↓
Which group?

ORDER BY
    ↓
Which row is first?

FIRST_VALUE()
    ↓
Which column's value should I take from that first row?
```
